# escape-step: bodies on an origin that is illegal for their size (a 2x2 body straddling a wall's edge, as a unit
# completed on a spot a wreck or a yard covers).
# A: the straight step at its target leads into the wall, so the mover refuses it. The body used to try that one
# step again on every update and stand for good with its order; it now walks to the legal origin beside it and
# goes round the wall.
# P: the same body, but every legal origin beside it is covered by idle bodies of an ENEMY player (E). An
# enemy's bodies are never a reason to end an order: P keeps it for the whole run (5,400 ticks, past the long
# stand-down's 4,800).
# Keys: g.A.arrived (1; 0 before), g.P.complete_n (0), work.escape_steps.total.
